---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { BRAND, SITE_URL, absoluteUrl } from '../../lib/site';

const aboutSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: `About ${BRAND}`,
  url: absoluteUrl('/en/about/'),
  inLanguage: 'en-CH',
  publisher: { '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#organization` },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About | ${BRAND}`}
  description="Who is behind CalcSwiss and why these calculators exist: independent, ad-free and with a transparent methodology."
  path="/en/about/"
  locale="en"
  jsonLd={[aboutSchema]}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ name: 'About' }]} locale="en" />
  <article class="prose-content max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">About</h1>
    <p>
      CalcSwiss is an independent project with a simple goal: precise, free finance and tax calculators for
      Switzerland — no advertising, no data collection, no hidden brokerage interests.
    </p>

    <h2>Why CalcSwiss exists</h2>
    <p>
      Swiss taxes are complicated: 26 cantons, over 2,000 municipalities, each with its own schedules and multipliers.
      Good calculators exist, but many are either tied to a comparison portal with a brokerage interest or do not
      disclose how they calculate. We wanted an offering that does both differently: neutral and verifiable.
    </p>

    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Every figure has an official source.</strong> Our tax parameters come from the data of the Federal Tax
        Administration (FTA), social-insurance values from the federal government. All sources are listed under
        <a href="/en/sources/">Sources</a>, with their reference date.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We disclose the methodology.</strong> For each calculator we document the formulas, parameters and
        limits — read them under <a href="/en/methodology/">Methodology</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We test the calculations.</strong> Every tax formula is safeguarded by automated tests against
        reference values before it goes live.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We are neutral.</strong> No advertising, no cookies, no lead brokerage. We recommend no products and
        receive no commissions.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we are not</h2>
    <p>
      CalcSwiss is neither a comparison portal, nor a bank, nor a tax-advisory firm. Our calculators provide a
      well-founded orientation but do not replace individual advice. Binding is always the official assessment by the
      competent tax authority. For larger decisions — relocation, retirement, capital withdrawal — consulting a
      professional is worthwhile.
    </p>

    <h2>How current is the data?</h2>
    <p>
      The calculators work with the tariffs and rates of the current tax year; every calculator page states its data
      snapshot in the footer. When an authority publishes new values — the multipliers of a new year, adjusted pillar
      3a maximum amounts, new withholding tax tariffs — we update the affected data file, and with it every page that
      computes from it. The <a href="/en/sources/">sources</a> page lists the datasets in use with their retrieval
      dates in a table.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact and operator</h2>
    <p>
      CalcSwiss is operated by <strong>Thanakorn Praisee</strong>; the full operator details are in the
      <a href="/en/legal-notice/">legal notice</a>. Spotted an error or have feedback? Write to
      <a href="mailto:kontakt@calcswiss.ch">kontakt@calcswiss.ch</a> — we check every report against the official
      sources and fix confirmed errors with the next update.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
